"margin": 7.06, "lean": 1.0, "environment": 8.3, "incumbency": -2.0, "money": -0.24}, "rating_margin": 5.1, "sigma_race": 6.4, "sigma_total": 7.06, "baseline_margin": 5.88, "analyst_adjustment": 0.42, "key_factors": ["Redrawn district now leans Democratic and the midterm environment strongly favors Democrats", "Six of ten expert ratings call it a Democratic flip while Kalshi prices a Democratic win near 90%", "Valadao's incumbency and cash advantage ($3.4M to $0.6M) keep him competitive", "No public general-election polls; outside groups have spent heavily both for and against Villegas"], "rationale": "The redrawn D+1 district and a Democratic-tilting midterm environment outweigh Valadao's incumbency and fundraising edge; most expert ratings point to a narrow Democratic flip and Kalshi prices Democrats near ninety percent, though three raters still call it a tossup and no public polls exist.", "watch": "Fresh public polling or a decisive debate moment could move a race that currently rests on fundamentals rather than survey data.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent David Valadao (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent David Valadao is defending a Central Valley seat that California's redrawn map moved to a slight Democratic lean, and a favorable midterm environment has made it a prime Democratic pickup target. Six of ten expert ratings lean or likely Democratic, though Cook, Fox News, and Inside Elections still call it a tossup; Kalshi traders price a Democratic win near ninety percent.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the assessment rests on fundamentals. Valadao holds a large cash advantage, roughly $3.4 million to Randy Villegas's $0.6 million, while outside groups have spent heavily both supporting and opposing Villegas. Speaker Mike Johnson's Bakersfield rally and a Giffords PAC ad against Valadao underline how contested the seat remains. The race tilts to Villegas by a moderate margin, with uncertainty well above average given the lack of survey data.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7982, "margin": 5.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8298, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8404, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8532, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8134, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7945, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8475, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8189, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8075, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8433, "margin": 6.2}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8577, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8627, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8486, "margin": 6.3}]}